WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.350
Your blood stays between pH 7.35 and 7.45.

2
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.970
Sprint for a bus, and your muscles release
extra hydrogen ions into your blood.

3
00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:12.970
Yet the pH of your blood hardly moves.

4
00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:15.410
Your muscles have just added acid.

5
00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:20.570
So why does your blood stay at
about pH 7.4, even after a sprint?

6
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.350
In this mission, you'll meet buffers,

7
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.710
and find out how acidic
and basic buffers are made.

8
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:30.810
You'll calculate the pH of a buffer, and
see what happens when you dilute one.

9
00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:34.850
Your mission: explain how your
blood holds its pH steady.
